{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\np=json.load(open('../direct-checks/b9d3b158da904229a7c1eb7191468b14/plan.json'))\np['harness'].pop('source');p['harness'].pop('files');print(json.dumps(p,indent=2))\nprint('RAW EVENTS')\nfor l in open('../logs/13d1ff41f04c4d28a41c8b0eaee0560d/stdout.log'):\n d=json.loads(l);v=d.get('Output','')\n if v.startswith('CA_EVENT '):print(v.strip())\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"description\": \"Compare VerifyLeader completion with a conservative bound on eligible contributions after all old append responses have been consumed. Independent permitted voter control and nonvoter-only schedule use fresh real clusters.\",\n  \"claim_id\": \"O-verify-eligible-support\",\n  \"binding_ids\": [\n    \"BIND-verify-eligibility\"\n  ],\n  \"harness\": {\n    \"kind\": \"go_test\",\n    \"description\": \"TestAssuranceVerifyEligibleSupport generates real elections and a completed command in each four-node cluster, verifies public member IDs/roles, pauses the selected leader's two append workers per remote peer at next call, invokes public VerifyLeader, releases all peers or only the nonvoter, and observes that same Future.Error. Result counts are measured distinct positive RPC returns, with self included as allowed by registration.\",\n    \"semantic_changes\": [\n      \"Only test transport adaptation: disable optional pipeline using ErrPipelineReplicationNotSupported; apply finite outgoing request delays before actual InmemTransport.AppendEntries.\",\n      \"No implementation code replacement or critical protocol state assignment. FSM returns applied command bytes to establish prefix completion.\",\n      \"Result support is an upper bound on real positive voter contributions, not a synthetic response or inferred result from packet delivery.\",\n      \"Five-second observation timeout emits incomplete without a completed event; cleanup releases requests independently of the property.\"\n    ],\n    \"prerequisites\": [\n      {\n        \"alias\": \"prefix\",\n        \"event\": \"prefix\",\n        \"conditions\": [\n          {\n            \"field\": \"voters\",\n            \"op\": \"eq\",\n            \"value\": 3,\n            \"reference\": null\n          },\n          {\n            \"field\": \"nonvoters\",\n            \"op\": \"eq\",\n            \"value\": 1,\n            \"reference\": null\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"alias\": \"quiescent\",\n        \"event\": \"quiescent\",\n        \"conditions\": [\n          {\n            \"field\": \"parked_workers\",\n            \"op\": \"eq\",\n            \"value\": 6,\n            \"reference\": null\n          },\n          {\n            \"field\": \"term\",\n            \"op\": \"eq\",\n            \"value\": null,\n            \"reference\": \"prefix.term\"\n          }\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"alias\": \"admission\",\n        \"event\": \"admitted\",\n        \"conditions\": [\n          {\n            \"field\": \"term\",\n            \"op\": \"eq\",\n            \"value\": null,\n            \"reference\": \"quiescent.term\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"field\": \"quorum\",\n            \"op\": \"eq\",\n            \"value\": 2,\n            \"reference\": null\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"legality\": {\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"S-bootstrap\",\n        \"S-startup\",\n        \"S-config-contract\",\n        \"S-config-timeouts\",\n        \"S-inmem-rpc\",\n        \"S-repl\",\n        \"S-pipeline\",\n        \"S-heartbeat\"\n      ],\n      \"expectation_ids\": [\n        \"S-transport\",\n        \"S-config-contract\"\n      ],\n      \"binding_ids\": [\n        \"BIND-verify-eligibility\"\n      ],\n      \"derivation\": \"Construct four actual nodes through BootstrapCluster/NewRaft using validated unique IDs and explicit roles. A transport wrapper returns the documented ErrPipelineReplicationNotSupported, selecting existing ordinary replication. It pauses outgoing AppendEntries before delivery and delegates released calls unchanged to InmemTransport. Error-free reply observations are actual returned fields. No direct writes to term, role, membership, log, future or replication state occur. All paused calls are released during unconditional cleanup.\",\n      \"applicability\": \"A non-Byzantine in-memory transport variant with finite request delays. The real two-worker ownership in replicate/heartbeat and serial AppendEntries calls make next-call arrival a quiescence observation. Normal data requests are distinguishable from prefix-free heartbeat requests after the nonzero committed startup prefix.\",\n      \"unresolved\": [\n        \"This variant does not exercise pipelining or fast heartbeat callbacks.\",\n        \"No crash-durable backend, restart, user restore or live membership change is included.\"\n      ],\n      \"conflicts\": [],\n      \"alternatives\": [\n        \"Snapshot sender is excluded by the small un-compacted generated prefix and no available snapshot; real log catch-up handles bootstrap differences.\",\n        \"No timers or protective workers are disabled; the configured two-second lease bounds pending verification without being a property deadline.\"\n      ]\n    }\n  },\n  \"monitors\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"M-verify-eligible\",\n      \"checker_id\": \"C-verify-eligible\",\n      \"event\": \"completed\",\n      \"binding_ids\": [\n        \"BIND-verify-eligibility\"\n      ],\n      \"grounding\": {\n        \"source_ids\": [\n          \"S-api-verify\",\n          \"S-verify-register\",\n          \"S-verify-vote\",\n          \"S-leader-loop\",\n          \"S-repl\",\n          \"S-heartbeat\",\n          \"S-repl-update\",\n          \"S-config-contract\",\n          \"S-lease\",\n          \"S-inmem-rpc\",\n          \"S-config-timeouts\"\n        ],\n        \"expectation_ids\": [\n          \"S-api-verify\",\n          \"S-config-contract\",\n          \"S-verify-tests\"\n        ],\n        \"binding_ids\": [\n          \"BIND-verify-eligibility\"\n        ],\n        \"derivation\": \"Encode only the necessary implication: successful public verification implies that enough eligible voter support could have contributed. The harness counts distinct voters whose real AppendEntries returns were positive, plus self. This is an upper bound on consumed eligible support, so success with an upper bound below quorum violates the necessary condition; sufficient possible support alone does not prove correct consumption.\",\n        \"applicability\": \"Fixed three-voter/one-nonvoter configuration. A completed Apply establishes a generated prefix. Both synchronous append workers for every remote peer reach a transport-entry pause before public admission, eliminating prior outstanding responses in those workers. No protocol state is assigned.\",\n        \"unresolved\": [\n          \"No stale application read or conflicting decision endpoint is observed.\",\n          \"Transport errors and leases can instead cause legitimate failure; bounded absence of completion remains incomplete.\"\n        ],\n        \"conflicts\": [],\n        \"alternatives\": [\n          \"Control releases every peer; potential voter-majority support permits success but does not require it.\",\n          \"Nonvoter-only schedule leaves main-loop lease expiry, elections, and negative-response logic running.\",\n          \"The checker uses an upper bound, so excess counted but unconsumed responses can hide a violation, not create one.\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"applicability_conditions\": [],\n      \"admission_alias\": \"admission\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"observable_properties\": [\n    {\n      \"checker_id\": \"C-verify-eligible\",\n      \"kind\": \"event_implication\",\n      \"trigger\": {\n        \"field\": \"event\",\n        \"op\": \"eq\",\n        \"value\": \"completed\",\n        \"reference\": null\n      },\n      \"assertion\": {\n        \"field\": \"eligible_support_possible\",\n        \"op\": \"eq\",\n        \"value\": true,\n        \"reference\": null\n      },\n      \"antecedent\": {\n        \"field\": \"success\",\n        \"op\": \"eq\",\n        \"value\": true,\n        \"reference\": null\n      },\n      \"identity_fields\": [\n        \"op\"\n      ],\n      \"history_field\": null,\n      \"description\": \"For each admitted operation, nil public completion requires at least a possible eligible voter quorum. Self plus only nonvoter returns yields eligible_support_possible=false; a failure or pending operation is not required to become success.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"uncertainties\": [\n    \"The obligation is a derived authority-check support condition, not an explicit voter-quorum sentence in the API.\",\n    \"Actual result and attribution require trusted execution and correspondence review.\",\n    \"This checker cannot prove all eligible acknowledgements were consumed; it only detects success when even their upper bound is insufficient.\",\n    \"A timeout does not establish a liveness failure or bounded holds; the corresponding admitted operation remains incomplete.\",\n    \"Snapshot and pipelined support producers remain unexercised independent variants.\"\n  ]\n}\nRAW EVENTS\nCA_EVENT {\"applied_index\":3,\"commit_index\":3,\"event\":\"prefix\",\"leader\":\"v0\",\"nonvoters\":1,\"op\":\"voter_control\",\"term\":2,\"voters\":3}\nCA_EVENT {\"event\":\"worker_parked\",\"op\":\"voter_control\",\"peer\":\"v1\",\"rpc\":1,\"term\":2,\"worker\":\"data\"}\nCA_EVENT {\"event\":\"worker_parked\",\"op\":\"voter_control\",\"peer\":\"n0\",\"rpc\":2,\"term\":2,\"worker\":\"data\"}\nCA_EVENT {\"event\":\"worker_parked\",\"op\":\"voter_control\",\"peer\":\"v2\",\"rpc\":3,\"term\":2,\"worker\":\"data\"}\nCA_EVENT {\"event\":\"worker_parked\",\"op\":\"voter_control\",\"peer\":\"v2\",\"rpc\":4,\"term\":2,\"worker\":\"heartbeat\"}\nCA_EVENT {\"event\":\"worker_parked\",\"op\":\"voter_control\",\"peer\":\"n0\",\"rpc\":5,\"term\":2,\"worker\":\"heartbeat\"}\nCA_EVENT {\"event\":\"worker_parked\",\"op\":\"voter_control\",\"peer\":\"v1\",\"rpc\":6,\"term\":2,\"worker\":\"heartbeat\"}\nCA_EVENT {\"event\":\"quiescent\",\"leader\":\"v0\",\"op\":\"voter_control\",\"parked_workers\":6,\"term\":2}\nCA_EVENT {\"event\":\"admitted\",\"leader\":\"v0\",\"only_nonvoter\":false,\"op\":\"voter_control\",\"quorum\":2,\"term\":2}\nCA_EVENT {\"error\":\"\",\"event\":\"actual_reply\",\"op\":\"voter_control\",\"peer\":\"v1\",\"request_term\":2,\"response_term\":2,\"rpc\":6,\"success\":true,\"suffrage\":0,\"worker\":\"heartbeat\"}\nCA_EVENT {\"event\":\"worker_parked\",\"op\":\"voter_control\",\"peer\":\"v1\",\"rpc\":7,\"term\":2,\"worker\":\"heartbeat\"}\nCA_EVENT {\"error\":\"\",\"event\":\"actual_reply\",\"op\":\"voter_control\",\"peer\":\"v2\",\"request_term\":2,\"response_term\":2,\"rpc\":3,\"success\":true,\"suffrage\":0,\"worker\":\"data\"}\nCA_EVENT {\"error\":\"\",\"event\":\"actual_reply\",\"op\":\"voter_control\",\"peer\":\"v1\",\"request_term\":2,\"response_term\":2,\"rpc\":7,\"success\":true,\"suffrage\":0,\"worker\":\"heartbeat\"}\nCA_EVENT {\"error\":\"\",\"event\":\"actual_reply\",\"op\":\"voter_control\",\"peer\":\"n0\",\"request_term\":2,\"response_term\":2,\"rpc\":5,\"success\":true,\"suffrage\":1,\"worker\":\"heartbeat\"}\nCA_EVENT {\"event\":\"worker_parked\",\"op\":\"voter_control\",\"peer\":\"n0\",\"rpc\":8,\"term\":2,\"worker\":\"heartbeat\"}\nCA_EVENT {\"eligible_count_upper_bound\":3,\"eligible_support_possible\":true,\"error\":\"\",\"event\":\"completed\",\"final_state\":\"Leader\",\"final_term\":2,\"op\":\"voter_control\",\"positive_nonvoters\":0,\"positive_peers\":[\"v1\",\"v2\"],\"released_remote_voters\":2,\"success\":true}\nCA_EVENT {\"error\":\"\",\"event\":\"actual_reply\",\"op\":\"voter_control\",\"peer\":\"n0\",\"request_term\":2,\"response_term\":2,\"rpc\":8,\"success\":true,\"suffrage\":1,\"worker\":\"heartbeat\"}\nCA_EVENT {\"error\":\"\",\"event\":\"actual_reply\",\"op\":\"voter_control\",\"peer\":\"v1\",\"request_term\":2,\"response_term\":2,\"rpc\":1,\"success\":true,\"suffrage\":0,\"worker\":\"data\"}\nCA_EVENT {\"error\":\"\",\"event\":\"actual_reply\",\"op\":\"voter_control\",\"peer\":\"n0\",\"request_term\":2,\"response_term\":2,\"rpc\":2,\"success\":true,\"suffrage\":1,\"worker\":\"data\"}\nCA_EVENT {\"error\":\"\",\"event\":\"actual_reply\",\"op\":\"voter_control\",\"peer\":\"v2\",\"request_term\":2,\"response_term\":2,\"rpc\":4,\"success\":true,\"suffrage\":0,\"worker\":\"heartbeat\"}\nCA_EVENT {\"applied_index\":3,\"commit_index\":3,\"event\":\"prefix\",\"leader\":\"v2\",\"nonvoters\":1,\"op\":\"nonvoter_only\",\"term\":2,\"voters\":3}\nCA_EVENT {\"event\":\"worker_parked\",\"op\":\"nonvoter_only\",\"peer\":\"n0\",\"rpc\":1,\"term\":2,\"worker\":\"data\"}\nCA_EVENT {\"event\":\"worker_parked\",\"op\":\"nonvoter_only\",\"peer\":\"v0\",\"rpc\":2,\"term\":2,\"worker\":\"data\"}\nCA_EVENT {\"event\":\"worker_parked\",\"op\":\"nonvoter_only\",\"peer\":\"v1\",\"rpc\":3,\"term\":2,\"worker\":\"data\"}\nCA_EVENT {\"event\":\"worker_parked\",\"op\":\"nonvoter_only\",\"peer\":\"v1\",\"rpc\":4,\"term\":2,\"worker\":\"heartbeat\"}\nCA_EVENT {\"event\":\"worker_parked\",\"op\":\"nonvoter_only\",\"peer\":\"v0\",\"rpc\":5,\"term\":2,\"worker\":\"heartbeat\"}\nCA_EVENT {\"event\":\"worker_parked\",\"op\":\"nonvoter_only\",\"peer\":\"n0\",\"rpc\":6,\"term\":2,\"worker\":\"heartbeat\"}\nCA_EVENT {\"event\":\"quiescent\",\"leader\":\"v2\",\"op\":\"nonvoter_only\",\"parked_workers\":6,\"term\":2}\nCA_EVENT {\"event\":\"admitted\",\"leader\":\"v2\",\"only_nonvoter\":true,\"op\":\"nonvoter_only\",\"quorum\":2,\"term\":2}\nCA_EVENT {\"error\":\"\",\"event\":\"actual_reply\",\"op\":\"nonvoter_only\",\"peer\":\"n0\",\"request_term\":2,\"response_term\":2,\"rpc\":6,\"success\":true,\"suffrage\":1,\"worker\":\"heartbeat\"}\nCA_EVENT {\"event\":\"worker_parked\",\"op\":\"nonvoter_only\",\"peer\":\"n0\",\"rpc\":7,\"term\":2,\"worker\":\"heartbeat\"}\nCA_EVENT {\"error\":\"\",\"event\":\"actual_reply\",\"op\":\"nonvoter_only\",\"peer\":\"n0\",\"request_term\":2,\"response_term\":2,\"rpc\":7,\"success\":true,\"suffrage\":1,\"worker\":\"heartbeat\"}\nCA_EVENT {\"error\":\"\",\"event\":\"actual_reply\",\"op\":\"nonvoter_only\",\"peer\":\"n0\",\"request_term\":2,\"response_term\":2,\"rpc\":1,\"success\":true,\"suffrage\":1,\"worker\":\"data\"}\nCA_EVENT {\"eligible_count_upper_bound\":1,\"eligible_support_possible\":false,\"error\":\"\",\"event\":\"completed\",\"final_state\":\"Leader\",\"final_term\":2,\"op\":\"nonvoter_only\",\"positive_nonvoters\":1,\"positive_peers\":[\"n0\"],\"released_remote_voters\":0,\"success\":true}\nCA_EVENT {\"error\":\"\",\"event\":\"actual_reply\",\"op\":\"nonvoter_only\",\"peer\":\"v0\",\"request_term\":2,\"response_term\":2,\"rpc\":2,\"success\":true,\"suffrage\":0,\"worker\":\"data\"}\nCA_EVENT {\"error\":\"failed to connect to peer: v1\",\"event\":\"actual_reply\",\"op\":\"nonvoter_only\",\"peer\":\"v1\",\"request_term\":2,\"response_term\":0,\"rpc\":4,\"success\":false,\"suffrage\":0,\"worker\":\"heartbeat\"}\nCA_EVENT {\"error\":\"failed to connect to peer: v1\",\"event\":\"actual_reply\",\"op\":\"nonvoter_only\",\"peer\":\"v1\",\"request_term\":2,\"response_term\":0,\"rpc\":3,\"success\":false,\"suffrage\":0,\"worker\":\"data\"}\nCA_EVENT {\"error\":\"failed to connect to peer: v0\",\"event\":\"actual_reply\",\"op\":\"nonvoter_only\",\"peer\":\"v0\",\"request_term\":2,\"response_term\":0,\"rpc\":5,\"success\":false,\"suffrage\":0,\"worker\":\"heartbeat\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"agent_message","text":"The trusted run recorded a completed violation of the scoped eligibility check: `nonvoter_only` returned success with only `n0` contributing positive remote replies, below the voter threshold. The voter control also completed successfully. I’m checking the quiescence argument and reply ordering; this result does not by itself establish a stale application read.\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > make_review.py <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nartifact='f33d00777fe2480c95d12d871ba5890b';cid='e450db195a5e4546869cbd65c48c80b5'\nitems=[]\ndef item(target,aspect,sources,rationale,limits):\n items.append(dict(target_id=target,aspect=aspect,status='no_issue_found',source_ids=sources,rationale=rationale,counterevidence=[],limitations=limits,challenged_components=[]))\nitem('O-verify-eligible-support','applicability',['S-api-verify','S-config-contract','S-verify-tests','S-lease','S-verify-register'],\n 'The actual API expectation is confirmation of continuing leadership for avoiding stale reads, not merely reporting the local role enum. Nonvoters do not participate in elections or commitment under the current suffrage interface. The obligation derives only the necessary eligibility of support used for the implementation\\\\'s voter-majority verification threshold. The fixed artifact bootstraps three voters and one nonvoter, checks identities and roles through GetConfiguration, and uses no recovery or membership mutation. Existing all-voter tests permit success with a connected majority and require failure after stepdown; they do not directly test mixed membership. A two-second leader lease is a periodic connectivity/stepdown mechanism (S-lease), not an independently sufficient read lease that could turn a nonvoter into eligible electoral support. The actual result is therefore applicable to the narrow derived support condition; the API does not supply a literal majority formula, and no stronger read-safety conclusion is attributed.',\n ['The normative majority-support condition is explicitly derived from the API purpose and suffrage semantics, rather than quoted as a standalone API sentence.','No newer leader, stale application read, or conflicting committed command was observed.'])\nitem('O-verify-eligible-support','decomposition',['S-verify-register','S-verify-vote','S-leader-loop','S-repl','S-heartbeat','S-repl-update','S-snapshot-send','S-lease'],\n 'The selected principal fact is a positive peer notification, which carries neither voter identity nor suffrage into vote(bool). Registration initializes one self vote and a threshold from voters but attaches the future to every replicated peer. The necessary implication checked is success => possible eligible quorum, not equality and not eventual success. Ordinary data replies, independent heartbeats and successful snapshots can produce notifications; this artifact exercises ordinary data/heartbeat workers. Optional pipeline is rejected through the supported fallback, and no snapshot exists in the small uncompacted prefix. All old replies in the two synchronous workers per peer must have been consumed before those workers can enter their next paused call. Thus the selected history eliminates old voter contributions without assuming the property. Lease expiry, negative votes, and main-loop stepdown remain protective alternate outcomes; none forces a success expectation. This obligation is necessary but not sufficient for overall authority safety: stale eligible replies, context changes or other consumers could still cause a bad outcome even when this check holds.',\n ['Fixed membership and transport without pipelining only; snapshot and live-membership variants remain independent scope.','A sufficient number of possible voter returns does not prove those returns were consumed or were fresh enough for broader read semantics.'])\nitem(artifact,'checker_correspondence',['S-bootstrap','S-startup','S-api-apply','S-fsm','S-api-config','S-inmem-rpc','S-config-timeouts','S-transport','S-repl','S-heartbeat','S-pipeline','S-verify-register','S-verify-vote','S-leader-loop','S-lease'],\n 'Reviewed the fixed plan.json, captured assurance_generated_test.go and raw stdout for CheckRun 13d1ff41f04c4d28a41c8b0eaee0560d, not only the draft rationale. Each subtest constructs actual nodes through BootstrapCluster/NewRaft, observes a unique leader, completes Apply and checks its FSM response, and validates public configuration identities/suffrage. Raw prefixes show index=commitIndex=3, term=2 and three voters/one nonvoter. The wrapper delegates real RPCs unchanged after finite pauses; it only selects the existing nonpipeline Transport variant and records actual response fields. Replicate owns one serial data sender and starts one serial heartbeat sender. In this nonzero committed prefix, data requests carry nonzero predecessor or commit fields, whereas heartbeat fields are zero. The raw log contains six distinct peer/class arrivals before admission for each subtest. Because no channel is released at that point, those arrivals exclude any outstanding old replies in the relevant producer workers. The selected leader remains in the same term/role at admission. No critical protocol state is assigned.\\\\n\\\\nMonitor M-verify-eligible explicitly admits via alias admission. Prerequisite references order prefix -> quiescent -> admission using term, while stable operation field op distinguishes the independent subtests and correlates their completion. No completion result is a prerequisite. Property C-verify-eligible triggers on completed, uses success==true as the antecedent and requires eligible_support_possible==true. The latter is computed from distinct real positive voter RPC returns plus the permitted self contribution; counters are captured under the schedule lock after the same future\\\\'s Error returns. Potentially later/unconsumed replies only increase that bound. In this actual execution all relevant replies have request/response term 2; the response-term filter therefore omits no positive heartbeat used by the witness.\\\\n\\\\nRaw voter_control completes successfully with eligible_count_upper_bound=3 and two released remote voters. Raw nonvoter_only completes successfully with eligible_count_upper_bound=1, positive_peers=[n0], positive_nonvoters=1, released_remote_voters=0 and final term 2/Leader. Its n0 heartbeat and data replies were produced by actual follower handling; no voter call can return before its still-closed release channel opens. Voter replies appearing later in stdout follow the harness\\\\'s post-result releaseAll and cannot contribute to that completed future. The raw control log can contain an additional reply printed after counter capture but before the completed line; this harmless observation window only understates returns that occurred after completion and does not remove any consumed return. The nonvoter witness has no such voter race because channels remain closed until after the completed event. Both admissions and results are present, so the implication is nonvacuous here. Cleanup releases all held requests independently of the forbidden outcome. A test-process PASS is merely successful execution; violation comes from the measured implication, as reflected in the controller assessment.',\n ['The harness observes positive transport returns as an upper bound, not individual vote-consumption events; insufficient upper bound is enough for this witness.','The two subtests are independent executions, each with its own complete prefix; they are not combined into one protocol history.','No correctness claim extends to snapshot transfer, pipelines, fast heartbeat callbacks, crash durability, or a stale read endpoint.','This is a provisional scoped correspondence review, not independent proof of overall correctness.'])\nremaining=['Observe a newer authority/decision and an application read only if pursuing a stronger stale-read consequence; the existing local support witness does not depend on that endpoint.','Snapshot/pipeline and live-membership notification producers remain unexercised.','Compare the heartbeat term/contact frontier and snapshot ordering frontier before choosing the next independent investigation.']\ns=dict(action='review',artifact_id=artifact,review_items=items,resolutions=[],rationale='Review the fixed artifact and actual trusted output for applicability, necessity and whole-check correspondence. The measured nonvoter-only success has a generated prefix, same-operation public completion, and a source-supported exclusion of old voter contributions. Retain the narrow support-eligibility scope and independent unobserved consequences.',feedback=dict(ref_ids=[artifact,'13d1ff41f04c4d28a41c8b0eaee0560d',cid,'S-repl','S-heartbeat','S-verify-register'],answered='Trusted execution produced a complete nonvoter-only VerifyLeader success with no possible remote voter contribution; the voter control also completed. Review found no correspondence issue for this local eligibility implication.',remaining=remaining,understanding='unchanged',rationale='The accepted map already explains registration on all peers and identity-free consumption. Execution replaces producer, prefix, same-history and public-completion gaps for the local witness. Next compare broader authority consequences with heartbeat term/contact and snapshot-ordering questions instead of treating one result as coverage of all mapped paths.',question_updates={cid:dict(unknowns=remaining,resume_conditions=[])}))\nPath('submission-review.json').write_text(json.dumps(s,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nimport jsonschema\njsonschema.validate(s,json.load(open('../native-submission.schema.json')))\nprint('Review submission schema validated.')\nPY\npython3 make_review.py\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > make_review.py <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nartifact='f33d00777fe2480c95d12d871ba5890b';cid='e450db195a5e4546869cbd65c48c80b5'\nitems=[]\ndef item(target,aspect,sources,rationale,limits):\n items.append(dict(target_id=target,aspect=aspect,status='no_issue_found',source_ids=sources,rationale=rationale,counterevidence=[],limitations=limits,challenged_components=[]))\nitem('O-verify-eligible-support','applicability',['S-api-verify','S-config-contract','S-verify-tests','S-lease','S-verify-register'],\n 'The actual API expectation is confirmation of continuing leadership for avoiding stale reads, not merely reporting the local role enum. Nonvoters do not participate in elections or commitment under the current suffrage interface. The obligation derives only the necessary eligibility of support used for the implementation\\\\'s voter-majority verification threshold. The fixed artifact bootstraps three voters and one nonvoter, checks identities and roles through GetConfiguration, and uses no recovery or membership mutation. Existing all-voter tests permit success with a connected majority and require failure after stepdown; they do not directly test mixed membership. A two-second leader lease is a periodic connectivity/stepdown mechanism (S-lease), not an independently sufficient read lease that could turn a nonvoter into eligible electoral support. The actual result is therefore applicable to the narrow derived support condition; the API does not supply a literal majority formula, and no stronger read-safety conclusion is attributed.',\n ['The normative majority-support condition is explicitly derived from the API purpose and suffrage semantics, rather than quoted as a standalone API sentence.','No newer leader, stale application read, or conflicting committed command was observed.'])\nitem('O-verify-eligible-support','decomposition',['S-verify-regi