tual nodes through BootstrapCluster/NewRaft, observes a unique leader, completes Apply and checks its FSM response, and validates public configuration identities/suffrage. Raw prefixes show index=commitIndex=3, term=2 and three voters/one nonvoter. The wrapper delegates real RPCs unchanged after finite pauses; it only selects the existing nonpipeline Transport variant and records actual response fields. Replicate owns one serial data sender and starts one serial heartbeat sender. In this nonzero committed prefix, data requests carry nonzero predecessor or commit fields, whereas heartbeat fields are zero. The raw log contains six distinct peer/class arrivals before admission for each subtest. Because no channel is released at that point, those arrivals exclude any outstanding old replies in the relevant producer workers. The selected leader remains in the same term/role at admission. No critical protocol state is assigned.\\\\n\\\\nMonitor M-verify-eligible explicitly admits via alias admission. Prerequisite references order prefix -> quiescent -> admission using term, while stable operation field op distinguishes the independent subtests and correlates their completion. No completion result is a prerequisite. Property C-verify-eligible triggers on completed, uses success==true as the antecedent and requires eligible_support_possible==true. The latter is computed from distinct real positive voter RPC returns plus the permitted self contribution; counters are captured under the schedule lock after the same future\\\\'s Error returns. Potentially later/unconsumed replies only increase that bound. In this actual execution all relevant replies have request/response term 2; the response-term filter therefore omits no positive heartbeat used by the witness.\\\\n\\\\nRaw voter_control completes successfully with eligible_count_upper_bound=3 and two released remote voters. Raw nonvoter_only completes successfully with eligible_count_upper_bound=1, positive_peers=[n0], positive_nonvoters=1, released_remote_voters=0 and final term 2/Leader. Its n0 heartbeat and data replies were produced by actual follower handling; no voter call can return before its still-closed release channel opens. Voter replies appearing later in stdout follow the harness\\\\'s post-result releaseAll and cannot contribute to that completed future. The raw control log can contain an additional reply printed after counter capture but before the completed line; this harmless observation window only understates returns that occurred after completion and does not remove any consumed return. The nonvoter witness has no such voter race because channels remain closed until after the completed event. Both admissions and results are present, so the implication is nonvacuous here. Cleanup releases all held requests independently of the forbidden outcome. A test-process PASS is merely successful execution; violation comes from the measured implication, as reflected in the controller assessment.',\n ['The harness observes positive transport returns as an upper bound, not individual vote-consumption events; insufficient upper bound is enough for this witness.','The two subtests are independent executions, each with its own complete prefix; they are not combined into one protocol history.','No correctness claim extends to snapshot transfer, pipelines, fast heartbeat callbacks, crash durability, or a stale read endpoint.','This is a provisional scoped correspondence review, not independent proof of overall correctness.'])\nremaining=['Observe a newer authority/decision and an application read only if pursuing a stronger stale-read consequence; the existing local support witness does not depend on that endpoint.','Snapshot/pipeline and live-membership notification producers remain unexercised.','Compare the heartbeat term/contact frontier and snapshot ordering frontier before choosing the next independent investigation.']\ns=dict(action='review',artifact_id=artifact,review_items=items,resolutions=[],rationale='Review the fixed artifact and actual trusted output for applicability, necessity and whole-check correspondence. The measured nonvoter-only success has a generated prefix, same-operation public completion, and a source-supported exclusion of old voter contributions. Retain the narrow support-eligibility scope and independent unobserved consequences.',feedback=dict(ref_ids=[artifact,'13d1ff41f04c4d28a41c8b0eaee0560d',cid,'S-repl','S-heartbeat','S-verify-register'],answered='Trusted execution produced a complete nonvoter-only VerifyLeader success with no possible remote voter contribution; the voter control also completed. Review found no correspondence issue for this local eligibility implication.',remaining=remaining,understanding='unchanged',rationale='The accepted map already explains registration on all peers and identity-free consumption. Execution replaces producer, prefix, same-history and public-completion gaps for the local witness. Next compare broader authority consequences with heartbeat term/contact and snapshot-ordering questions instead of treating one result as coverage of all mapped paths.',question_updates={cid:dict(unknowns=remaining,resume_conditions=[])}))\nPath('submission-review.json').write_text(json.dumps(s,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nimport jsonschema\njsonschema.validate(s,json.load(open('../native-submission.schema.json')))\nprint('Review submission schema validated.')\nPY\npython3 make_review.py\"","aggregated_output":"Review submission schema validated.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
